# AgriChain AI — Final Freeze & Submission Consistency Audit

We have completed Phase 20. The final submission deadline is November 7, 2026.

Your task is to perform a FINAL FREEZE AUDIT. Do not expand the project, retrain models, replace checkpoints, migrate databases, or redesign the frontend.

## 1. Freeze the implementation
- Preserve all five verified model checkpoints and their SHA-256 hashes.
- Preserve existing APIs, role-based dashboards, shipment workflows and file-based persistence.
- Do not introduce PostgreSQL/PostGIS runtime dependencies at this stage.
- Do not remove working features.

## 2. Verify the demonstration workflows
Verify:
- Farmer: manual fruit selection, automatic fruit identification and inspection.
- Logistics: shipment creation, route map and simulated telemetry.
- Dealer: intake and quality workflow.
- Buyer: marketplace and demo order creation.
- Admin: model registry, system health and CUDA diagnostics.

Confirm that Mango remains honestly gated and Apple remains detection-only.

## 3. Verify persistence
- Create a test shipment.
- Advance simulated telemetry.
- Restart the backend.
- Confirm shipment and telemetry records survive.
- Explicitly identify JSON file-based persistence as the active implementation.
- Do not claim live PostgreSQL/PostGIS integration.

## 4. Documentation consistency
Review:
- README
- Final architecture documentation
- Phase 19 report
- Phase 20 database verification report
- Final submission checklist
- Model and dataset licensing information

Correct inconsistent Windows edition/version information using actual runtime evidence.

Use accurate terminology:
- Active: JSON-based persistent ledger.
- Prepared but inactive: PostgreSQL/PostGIS deployment schema.
- Simulated: GPS and cold-chain telemetry.
- Demo-only: marketplace transactions.

## 5. Final deliverables
Create:
- docs/FINAL_DEMO_RUNBOOK.md
- docs/FINAL_VIVA_PREPARATION.md
- docs/FINAL_SUBMISSION_FREEZE_REPORT.md

The demo runbook should contain startup commands, URLs, demonstration order, sample workflows and troubleshooting.

The viva preparation should explain system architecture, CNNs, MobileNetV3, ResNet18, YOLOv8, model registry, confidence thresholds, LSTM spoilage-risk prediction, FastAPI, Next.js, file-based persistence, PostGIS architecture, simulated telemetry and model limitations.

## 6. Final regression
Run existing backend and frontend tests, Next.js production build and checkpoint hash verification.

Report actual results. Never fabricate successful tests or claim a feature was verified if it was not.

